# ONE FIELD, AND ONLY TO READ AND SET IT. GameRenderer.zoom scales the world's
# projection about the centre of the screen; it exists for huge screenshots
# and sits at 1 otherwise. Zoom sets it while the key is held. The field of
# view option cannot do this job: it rejects anything under 30 degrees and
# falls back to its default, so a 4x zoom at 70 came out as 70. See
# Behaviours.zoom. Nothing here injects code into a Minecraft method.
accessible field net/minecraft/client/render/GameRenderer zoom F

# AND THE HURT FLASH'S TEXTURE. OverlayTexture keeps the 16x16 image every
# entity is drawn with; its top half is the red a hit flashes. Hit colour
# repaints those pixels and uploads them again. See HitColour.
accessible field net/minecraft/client/render/OverlayTexture texture Lnet/minecraft/client/texture/NativeImageBackedTexture;
